prisoners survived because no drug entered their veins. But Pike received the drug pentobarbital.", "Officials do not know why the execution failed. They have not said if they will try again. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee stopped all executions for the rest of the year. The head of prisons in Tennessee plans to resign. Pike's lawyers will go to court in Nashville on Wednesday.", "Pike was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Pike was 18 years old at the time. Dr Joel Zivot is a doctor helping Pike's defence team. He said most people die from lethal injection. He said Pike's recovery is unusual, but there are still many unknowns."], "paragraphs_zh": ["50岁的克里斯塔·派克在田纳西州的一家医院里。她被铐在床上。她的律师周二说，她已经苏醒并且能说话。她仍然需要重症医疗护理。上周三，她挺过了两次失败的注射死刑。她昏迷了好几天。", "专家说这非常不寻常。黛博拉·丹诺是福特汉姆法学院的一名教授。她说，派克能醒来并说话让她“绝对震惊”。据信，派克是唯一一个在注射死刑中活下来的人。在另外七起案例中，囚犯活下来是因为没有药物进入他们的血管。但派克被注射了戊巴比妥。", "官员们不知道处决为什么失败。他们还没有说是否会再次尝试。田纳西州州长比尔·李停止了今年剩下的所有处决。田纳西州的监狱负责人计划辞职。派克的律师周三将在纳什维尔出庭。", "派克因在1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默而被判处死刑。当时派克18岁。乔尔·齐沃特医生是帮助派克辩护团队的医生。他说大多数人会死于注射死刑。他说派克的康复很不寻常，但仍有许多未知数。"], "body": "Christa Pike, 50, is in a hospital in Tennessee. She is handcuffed to the bed. Her lawyers said on Tuesday that she is awake and speaking. She still needs critical medical care. Last Wednesday, she survived two failed lethal injections. She was unconscious for days.\n\nExperts say this is very unusual. Deborah Denno is a professor at Fordham Law School. She said she was 'absolutely astonished' that Pike is awake and talking. Pike is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection. In seven other cases, prisoners survived because no drug entered their veins. But Pike received the drug pentobarbital.\n\nOfficials do not know why the execution failed. They have not said if they will try again. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee stopped all executions for the rest of the year. The head of prisons in Tennessee plans to resign. Pike's lawyers will go to court in Nashville on Wednesday.\n\nPike was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Pike was 18 years old at the time. Dr Joel Zivot is a doctor helping Pike's defence team. He said most people die from lethal injection. He said Pike's recovery is unusual, but there are still many unknowns.", "body_zh": "50岁的克里斯塔·派克在田纳西州的一家医院里。她被铐在床上。她的律师周二说，她已经苏醒并且能说话。她仍然需要重症医疗护理。上周三，她挺过了两次失败的注射死刑。她昏迷了好几天。\n\n专家说这非常不寻常。黛博拉·丹诺是福特汉姆法学院的一名教授。她说，派克能醒来并说话让她“绝对震惊”。据信，派克是唯一一个在注射死刑中活下来的人。在另外七起案例中，囚犯活下来是因为没有药物进入他们的血管。但派克被注射了戊巴比妥。\n\n官员们不知道处决为什么失败。他们还没有说是否会再次尝试。田纳西州州长比尔·李停止了今年剩下的所有处决。田纳西州的监狱负责人计划辞职。派克的律师周三将在纳什维尔出庭。\n\n派克因在1995年谋杀科琳·斯莱默而被判处死刑。当时派克18岁。乔尔·齐沃特医生是帮助派克辩护团队的医生。他说大多数人会死于注射死刑。他说派克的康复很不寻常，但仍有许多未知数。", "text": "Christa Pike, 50, is in a hospital in Tennessee. She is handcuffed to the bed. Her lawyers said on Tuesday that she is awake and speaking. She still needs critical medical care. Last Wednesday, she survived two failed lethal injections. She was unconscious for days. Experts say this is very unusual. Deborah Denno is a professor at Fordham Law School. She said she was 'absolutely astonished' that Pike is awake and talking. Pike is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection. In seven other cases, prisoners survived because no drug entered their veins. But Pike received the drug pentobarbital. Officials do not know why the execution failed. They have not said if they will try again. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee stopped all executions for the rest of the year. The head of prisons in Tennessee plans to resign. Pike's lawyers will go to court in Nashville on Wednesday. Pike was sentenced to death for murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995. Pike was 18 years old at the time. Dr Joel Zivot is a doctor helping Pike's defence team. He said most people die from lethal injection. He said Pike's recovery is unusual, but there are still many unknowns.", "vocab": [{"word": "inmate", "pos": "noun", "zh": "囚犯", "note": "指监狱里的犯人"}, {"word": "death row", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "死囚牢房", "note": "等待处决的囚犯关押的地方"}, {"word": "execution", "pos": "noun", "zh": "处决", "note": "依法杀死囚犯"}, {"word": "lethal injection", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "注射死刑", "note": "用注射药物执行死刑"}, {"word": "survive", "pos": "verb", "zh": "幸存", "note": "在危险后仍然活着"}, {"word": "unconscious", "pos": "adj", "zh": "昏迷的", "note": "失去知觉"}, {"word": "lawyer", "pos": "noun", "zh": "律师", "note": "提供法律帮助的人"}, {"word": "hospital", "pos": "noun", "zh": "医院", "note": "治疗病人的地方"}], "title_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say", "summary_original": "Experts and lawyers called the apparent recovery unprecedented, noting she is believed to be the only known person to survive a lethal injection.", "body_original": "US death row inmate Christa Pike awake and speaking after failed execution, lawyers say\nBy\nSareen Habeshian\nand\nKwasi Gyamfi Asiedu\nPublished\n6 October 2026\nUpdated 57 minutes ago\nUS death row inmate Christa Pike is \"conscious and speaking\" after surviving a failed execution attempt last week, her lawyers say.\nPike, 50, continues to receive critical medical care while handcuffed in hospital, her attorneys said in a statement on Tuesday.\nPike, who was sentenced to death after murdering Colleen Slemmer in 1995, survived two failed lethal injections last Wednesday in Tennessee. She was taken to hospital, where she remained unconscious for days as medical staff cleared her body of the injected chemical.\nExperts and her legal team say her apparent recovery is unprecedented. She is believed to be the only person to survive a lethal injection.\nHer lawyers called her progress \"medically unprecedented\", and while her prognosis remains unclear, \"at a minimum, we expect a long recovery\".\nDeborah Denno, a criminologist and professor at Fordham Law School, said she was \"absolutely astonished\" that Pike is conscious and speaking.\nThere were seven other cases where prisoners survived slated executions, but in those cases, executioners were not able to inject anything into the inmates' veins, Denno told the BBC.\nPike \"is the only person for whom some kind of toxin has been injected,\" she said.\n\"They did everything they were supposed to do as part of the execution process, and it simply didn't work,\" Denno said. \"This has never happened before.\"\nAuthorities have not yet said whether they will try again to execute Pike. They have also not offered an explanation for what went wrong after injecting her with the chemical pentobarbital.\nTennessee Governor Bill Lee suspended all executions for the rest of the year - and the head of prisons in the state said over the weekend that he plans to resign.\nPike was 18 when she and her then-boyfriend, Tadaryl Shipp, beat, tortured and killed 19-year-old Slemmer, whom they had met at a job training camp for troubled teens.\nPike's attorneys are scheduled to appear in court in Nashville on Wednesday. They also plan to hold a news conference outside the court.\nDr Joel Zivot, an anaesthesiologist advising Pike's defence team, said on Tuesday that the likelihood of recovering from lethal injection is low.\n\"Most people who get lethal injection die from it,\" he told the BBC. \"In fact, pretty well everyone, except Christa. So, the fact that she survived it ... was unusual.\"\nBut there remains a lot of uncertainty and many unknowns, he said, including how much of the pentobarbital got into her system, what her blood levels were after the injection and what her recovery will look like.\n\"I would not, in any way, say at this point that all the big risks are behind her,\" he noted.\nZivot had previously said the two doses of pentobarbital she received last week would have been enough that, had it entered her bloodstream in normal circulation, \"she would have surely died\".\nInstead, Zivot said a possible explanation is that instead of entering Pike's bloodstream, the pentobarbital was more likely to have spread across the tissue under her skin.\nZivot said last week he thought her ending up with a brain injury was \"very possible\", due to the delays in resuscitating her. He also believed it would take about a week to truly understand her condition and do a neurological exam. It's now been six days since the failed attempt to execute her.\nPike's lawyers previously warned that her medical history and anatomy - including thrombocytosis (a blood-clotting condition) and small veins - meant there was a risk she would experience \"unnecessary\" pain and suffering during a lethal injection.\nThey said on Tuesday that she has endured \"severe damage\" to her arms.\nRelated topics\nTennessee\nCapital punishment\nUnited States\nMore on this story\nI interviewed Christa Pike 20 years ago - I can't stop thinking about her\nPublished\n3 days ago\nTennessee prison chief to resign after Christa Pike's failed execution\nPublished\n3 days ago\nWhat happened in the failed execution of Christa Pike - and what next?\nPublished\nJust now", "fetched_at": "2026-10-07T00:57:05.204052", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Christa", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.475, "sm": 100, "em": 475, "cs": 0, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Pike", "s": 0.487, "e": 0.787, "sm": 487, "em": 787, "cs": 8, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": ",", "s": 0.787, "e": 0.963, "sm": 787, "em": 962, "cs": 12, "ce": 13, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "50", "s": 0.963, "e": 1.425, "sm": 962, "em": 1425, "cs": 14, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": ",", "s": 1.425, "e": 1.562, "sm": 1425, "em": 1562, "cs": 16, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "is", "s": 1.562, "e": 1.675, "sm": 1562, "em": 1675, "cs": 18, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "in", "s": 1.688, "e": 1.775, "sm": 1687, "em": 1775, "cs": 21, "ce": 23, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "a", "s": 1.788, "e": 1.828, "sm": 1787, "em": 1827, "cs": 24, "ce": 25, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "hospital", "s": 1.837, "e": 2.375, "sm": 1837, "em": 2375, "cs": 26, "ce": 34, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "in", "s": 2.388, "e": 2.513, "sm": 2387, "em": 2512, "cs": 35, "ce": 37, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "Ten